--[[
        NEW SEEK -- DOORS' Seek with another body, and its glitched version

            _G.Type = "Normal"   -- or "Glitch"
            loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bonellocristian78-lab/Gradish-Mode/claude/sei-qui-con-noi-ye4k62/NewSeek"))()

        Every Seek that comes (SeekMovingNewClone, SeekMoving) wears the new one: DOORS' own is still there (the server
        moves it, its hit and its cutscenes are its own) but you see the new one in its place, moving joint by joint the
        way DOORS' moves (out of the floor, the run). If DOORS' joints are not the new one's, the new one plays its own
        animations (emerge, run, idle).

        Glitch: Seek made of DOORS' Glitch (ReplicatedStorage.Entities.Glitch). Its purple body under Glitch's cube
        texture, Glitch's cube particles (white, red, cyan), Glitch's pink light. Its eyes are glitched: Seek's eye and
        Glitch's cube in turns, cyan and pink. Its hands are clusters of cubes that never keep still. Cubes break off
        it all the time, its colours flicker, its limbs jump off their joints, it hangs a moment and snaps on, its
        sounds warble, and when it is close Glitch's cubes flash on your screen.

        Light on the game: nothing is made while it runs (its cubes are always the same few, moved), DOORS' Seek is
        hidden once (not every frame), no shadows from it, fewer goo particles.

        Only you see it. Run it again to change type; getgenv().__NewSeek() takes it off.
        Its model is assets/seek/NewSeek.rbxm, downloaded once into the executor's folder (NewSeek/).
]]

